---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import SiteNav from '../../components/SiteNav.astro';

const groups = [
  { id: 'start', title: 'Start with a product', intro: 'Finding, comparing and opening a product link.', items: [
    ['What is a LitBuy spreadsheet?', 'It is a product-discovery format that groups visible source titles, IDs, categories, images and CNY price references. This independent site uses FindSpreadsheet source records to help visitors research; it does not sell goods, accept payment, authenticate items or operate LitBuy.', 'Use a product card as a research starting point. Confirm the current option, price, availability and terms in the live LitBuy flow before paying.'],
    ['Can I use Taobao, Weidian or 1688 links with LitBuy?', 'LitBuy’s public order guidance says buyers can paste Taobao, Weidian and 1688 links into its search bar for order processing. Keep the source ID, option, colour, size and quantity in a note so you can compare them with the live order screen.', 'A saved link does not prove stock or that a future listing will match an earlier image or title. Recheck the live product before placing an order.'],
    ['Why can the USD amount differ from the final charge?', 'The original CNY amount is the source-listing reference. The USD number shown here is only an indicative browsing conversion, not a quote. Variant choice, service charges, parcel shipping, payment conversion, taxes and destination fees may all affect the final amount.', 'Use it to compare records, then rely on the live LitBuy order and parcel flow for current payable amounts.']
  ]},
  { id: 'qc', title: 'QC and warehouse review', intro: 'How to interpret inspection evidence without overclaiming.', items: [
    ['What can QC photos tell me?', 'LitBuy’s public materials describe a basic warehouse quality check and inspection photos when goods arrive. Order-specific photos can help check visible details such as colour, a size label, quantity, obvious marks or an included component.', 'They cannot establish authenticity, hidden defects, fit, durability, customs acceptance or a delivery outcome. Keep reference images separate from photos of your own order.'],
    ['What should I check in an inspection image?', 'Compare the visible item with your selected option: the variant name, colour, size label, quantity and the few details that mattered in your original choice. A short, item-specific checklist is more useful than a vague scan of many pictures.', 'If an angle cannot answer a question, do not guess. Record the order reference and ask about the exact visible point through the current LitBuy process.'],
    ['What should I do if something is unclear?', 'Pause before international parcel submission and create a factual note: product ID, selected option, relevant image and the visible point that needs clarification. Review the current official after-sales terms for the order.', 'Do not assume a refund, exchange or return is automatic; the available route can depend on policy, timing, item state and seller conditions.']
  ]},
  { id: 'shipping', title: 'Storage, parcels and tracking', intro: 'Planning an international shipment with current information.', items: [
    ['How do storage and consolidation work?', 'LitBuy publicly describes storage and the ability to ship orders together. Its home page currently advertises storage up to 120 days, with the first 90 days stated as free. Check the live notice and order status because limits and fees can change.', 'Before combining items, list IDs, quantities, warehouse status and item type. Route eligibility can vary by contents, carrier and destination.'],
    ['Is LitBuy shipping a fixed cost or delivery time?', 'No. Route availability, destination, contents, dimensions, actual or volumetric weight and carrier events can change price and timing. This site does not make a fixed shipping or delivery promise.', 'Review the current parcel options, restrictions and address before submission. Tracking helps follow a shipment but does not guarantee a delivery date or customs result.'],
    ['How do I handle restricted items, refunds or returns?', 'A catalogue appearance does not make an item eligible for every route. Transport limits can depend on carrier, destination and law. Read the current shipping information for the exact parcel contents.', 'For refunds and returns, use the current LitBuy policy and the order’s state as the source of truth. Keep your order and parcel identifiers until the shipment is resolved.']
  ]}
];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" /><meta name="description" content="Clear LitBuy spreadsheet FAQ covering product links, QC photos, storage and shipping." /><title>LitBuy Spreadsheet FAQ</title></head><body><SiteNav active="faq" /><main class="subpage faq-page"><p class="eyebrow">QUICK, FACT-LED ANSWERS</p><h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1><p class="lead">A simple three-step overview: find a product, review warehouse evidence, then decide about the parcel. Each card gives the answer first and the caution second.</p><nav class="faq-jump" aria-label="FAQ topics">{groups.map((group, index) => <a href={'#' + group.id}>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')} · {group.title}</a>)}</nav><div class="faq-topics">{groups.map((group, index) => <section class="faq-topic" id={group.id}><header><p class="eyebrow">STEP {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')} · {group.intro}</p><h2>{group.title}</h2></header><div class="faq-list page-faq">{group.items.map(([question, answer, caution]) => <article class="faq-answer-card"><h3>{question}</h3><p>{answer}</p><p class="faq-caution"><strong>Keep in mind:</strong> {caution}</p></article>)}</div></section>)}</div><aside class="faq-boundary"><strong>Independent research site.</strong> Internal browsing, search and product details stay here; LitBuy registration and final purchase are the only external actions. Policies, pricing, stock and route availability can change.</aside></main></body></html>
<style is:global>
.faq-page{max-width:940px}.faq-jump{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin:34px 0 48px}.faq-jump a{padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;background:#fff7f5;color:var(--ink);font-size:12px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}.faq-jump a:hover{border-color:var(--blue);color:var(--blue)}.faq-topics{display:grid;gap:28px}.faq-topic{padding:30px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:#fff}.faq-topic header{display:flex;align-items:end;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;padding-bottom:22px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.faq-topic header .eyebrow{margin:0;max-width:390px;line-height:1.55}.faq-topic h2{margin:0;font-size:clamp(27px,3vw,38px);letter-spacing:-.05em}.page-faq{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;margin-top:23px}.faq-answer-card{display:flex;min-height:100%;flex-direction:column;padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px;background:#fffaf8}.faq-answer-card h3{margin:0 0 13px;font-size:17px;letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.25}.faq-answer-card p{margin:0;color:var(--sub);font-size:13px;line-height:1.7}.faq-answer-card .faq-caution{margin-top:auto;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:12px}.faq-caution strong{color:var(--ink)}.faq-boundary{margin-top:34px;padding:18px 20px;border-radius:10px;background:#f3fbff;color:var(--sub);font-size:13px;line-height:1.65}.faq-boundary strong{color:var(--ink)}@media(max-width:700px){.page-faq{grid-template-columns:1fr}.faq-topic{padding:22px 18px}.faq-topic header{display:block}.faq-topic header .eyebrow{margin-bottom:9px}}
</style>
